1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Your spaceship just left without you,

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,600
and you're lost on a planet.

3
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:04,480
Let's rank four,

4
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:05,440
worst last.

5
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:06,240
Number four:

6
00:00:06,240 --> 00:00:07,040
Mercury.

7
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,720
With no real atmosphere,

8
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:10,640
the day side hits eight hundred degrees

9
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:11,520
Fahrenheit.

10
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:12,320
Then at night,

11
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:14,300
it drops to about minus two hundred

12
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:14,640
ninety.

13
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:15,440
You'd be cooked,

14
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:16,400
then frozen,

15
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:18,160
with no air to complain about it.

16
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:18,960
Number three:

17
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:19,760
Jupiter.

18
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:21,680
Jupiter has no ground at all,

19
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:23,760
only swirling gas and liquid,

20
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:25,360
getting denser as you sink.

21
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:26,400
You can't land.

22
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:27,040
You just fall,

23
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:28,400
and the pressure climbs.

24
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:29,200
Number two:

25
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:30,000
Neptune.

26
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,160
Neptune has no surface either,

27
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:33,760
and it's the windiest world in the

28
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:34,640
solar system.

29
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:36,640
Its winds top twelve hundred miles an

30
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:37,200
hour,

31
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,724
about nine times Earth's.

32
00:00:38,724 --> 00:00:40,324
Your hat would not survive.

33
00:00:40,324 --> 00:00:41,204
Number one:

34
00:00:41,204 --> 00:00:41,924
Venus.

35
00:00:41,924 --> 00:00:43,684
Venus has an actual ground,

36
00:00:43,684 --> 00:00:44,884
which sounds nice,

37
00:00:44,884 --> 00:00:46,164
until you stand on it.

38
00:00:46,164 --> 00:00:48,084
It's about eight hundred seventy degrees

39
00:00:48,084 --> 00:00:48,964
Fahrenheit,

40
00:00:48,964 --> 00:00:50,484
hot enough to melt lead.

41
00:00:50,484 --> 00:00:52,724
The air presses on you ninety-three times

42
00:00:52,724 --> 00:00:54,164
harder than on Earth,

43
00:00:54,164 --> 00:00:55,924
like a kilometer underwater,

44
00:00:55,924 --> 00:00:57,844
under sulfuric acid clouds.

45
00:00:57,844 --> 00:00:59,524
So where would you rather get lost?

46
00:00:59,524 --> 00:01:01,079
Please say Earth.

47
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:03,400
Like,

48
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:03,800
share,

49
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,690
and subscribe for more bad ideas.
